---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy — Weatherie"
	description="Privacy Policy for Weatherie app."
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
		<a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center text-sky-400 font-bold mb-12 hover:translate-x-[-4px] transition-transform">
			<svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path></svg>
			Back to Home
		</a>

		<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white mb-8 font-['Outfit']">Privacy Policy</h1>

		<div class="prose prose-invert prose-sky prose-lg text-slate-300 space-y-8">
			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Introduction</h2>
				<p>Your privacy matters to us. This Privacy Policy explains what information Weatherie ("we", "our", or "us") collects, how we use it, and who we share it with, when you use our mobile application and website. Weatherie is designed to work without an account — you are not asked to sign in or give us your name or email to use the app.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Information We Collect</h2>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
					<li><strong>Location.</strong> If you grant location permission, your device's coordinates are sent to our weather service to fetch the forecast for where you are. You can use the app without this by choosing a city manually. Location is used to serve your request and briefly cached to speed up nearby lookups — it is not tied to your identity or used to profile you.</li>
					<li><strong>Anonymous device identifier.</strong> To hold your purchases, credit balance, and unlocked themes without an account, we assign your install a random anonymous identifier. It is not linked to your name, email, or any advertising identifier.</li>
					<li><strong>Purchases.</strong> When you buy a credit pack or unlock a theme, the transaction is processed by the Apple App Store or Google Play and validated through RevenueCat. We receive a confirmation that the purchase occurred and its product identifier — never your card or payment details.</li>
					<li><strong>Diagnostic and technical data.</strong> Device type, operating-system version, and basic crash/diagnostic information, used to fix bugs and keep the app working.</li>
					<li><strong>Preferences.</strong> Your theme, units, and display settings are stored locally on your device.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">How We Use Information</h2>
				<p>We use the information above only to provide and improve Weatherie: to return the correct forecast, to remember what you have purchased and unlocked, to show relevant in-app promotions for our own apps, and to diagnose problems. We do not sell your personal information, and we do not track you across other companies' apps or websites for advertising.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Third-Party Services</h2>
				<p>We rely on a small number of service providers to run the app. Each has its own privacy policy:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
					<li><strong>OpenWeatherMap</strong> — supplies forecast data; receives location coordinates to answer a weather request.</li>
					<li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> — validates and manages purchases across the app stores.</li>
					<li><strong>Apple App Store / Google Play</strong> — process payments for in-app purchases.</li>
					<li><strong>Google Cloud</strong> — hosts our backend infrastructure.</li>
					<li><strong>Advection Software</strong> — serves the in-house cross-promotion for our own apps. These promotions do not use an advertising identifier and do not track you across other apps.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Your Choices</h2>
				<p>You can revoke location permission at any time in your device's settings, and the app will keep working with a manually chosen city. Because there is no account, you can remove the data associated with your install simply by uninstalling the app. You may also contact us to request deletion of any purchase records tied to your anonymous identifier.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Children's Privacy</h2>
				<p>Weatherie is a family-friendly application and is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us information, please contact us and we will delete it.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>We may update this Privacy Policy as the app evolves. Material changes will be reflected here with an updated date below.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Contact Us</h2>
				<p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@weatherie.com" class="text-sky-400 font-bold">contact@weatherie.com</a>.</p>
			</section>

			<p class="text-sm italic pt-8 border-t border-slate-700">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString()}</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
